      [
        "Performance Features",
        "1. One single drum can be fitted with three types of tanks to adapt to different separation processes.\n2. Semi‑countercurrent tank: suitable for wet roughing and cleaning of strongly magnetic minerals with particle size 0.5‑0 mm, especially for cleaning of 0.15～0 mm fine minerals.\n3. Counter‑current tank: suitable for wet roughing and scavenging of strongly magnetic minerals with particle size 0.6‑0 mm, especially for heavy‑medium recovery in coal washing plants.\n4. Downstream tank: suitable for roughing and cleaning of minerals with particle size 6‑0 mm.\n5. Semi‑countercurrent tanks and downstream tanks can be used in series to improve concentrate grade.\n6. The magnetic system is made of high‑quality ferrite or composite rare‑earth magnetic steel. Average magnetic induction intensity on drum surface ranges from 100 mT to 600 mT.\n7. Downstream, semi‑countercurrent and counter‑current types with different surface magnetic‑field strengths are available per customer requirements.",
        "",
